{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789853459,"nonce":"BhMyIzVybaXlhHhDak2aHNK/D/g=","title":"an enum stored in a Dynamic local comes back null","message":"`var d:Dynamic = A; name(d)` where `name(e:E)` switches on the enum prints `null`; `var d2:Dynamic = B(2)` likewise. The store boxes the enum as a reference (`haxe_box_reference_ptr`), and the call into an `E` parameter is meant to unbox it (`maybe_unbox_value` has an Enum arm over `haxe_unbox_reference_ptr`), yet the switch sees no variant. Reading the same value through a `Null\u003cE\u003e` source (`var d3:Dynamic = optA()`) works only because a `Null\u003creference\u003e` is deliberately left RAW when it enters a Dynamic slot (boxing.rs Optional arm) -- haxe.Template relies on that: `var eelse; eelse = parseBlock(..); run(eelse)`. Boxing it broke every `::else::` branch. When the enum round trip is fixed, the Optional arm can box every reference the way it boxes `Null\u003cString\u003e`.","files":null}]}